  "feesApplyText": "<p><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\"><strong>Fees for Assured Periodic Tenancy (APT)</strong></span><strong></strong></p><br /><p>\u00a0</p><br /><p><strong>Before You Move In</strong></p><br /><strong>Holding Deposit: </strong>Equivalent to one week\u2019s rent. This deposit holds the property while you complete reference checks and sign the tenancy agreement. If you cancel, provide false information, or don\u2019t complete the agreement, this deposit is not refunded.<br /><br /><p><strong><br />Security Deposit:</strong></p><br /><p><strong>For rent under \u00a350,000 per year:</strong> Five weeks\u2019 rent. This is held in a government-backed scheme and will be returned if there are no damages or unpaid rent.\u00a0<br /><strong>For rent between \u00a350,000 and \u00a3100,000 per year:</strong> Six weeks\u2019 rent, also held in a government-backed scheme.</p><br /><p>\u00a0</p><br /><p><strong>During Your Tenancy:</strong></p><br /><p><strong></strong><strong>Changing Your Contract: </strong>\u00a350 (inc. VAT) for any changes to the agreement, like altering the terms.</p><br /><p>\u00a0</p><br /><p><strong>Changing Tenants:</strong> \u00a350 (inc. VAT) per new tenant if someone leaves and you need a replacement. This covers new checks and paperwork.\u00a0</p><br /><p>\u00a0</p><br /><p><strong>Early Termination: </strong>If you want to leave early, you will need to pay the costs of finding a new tenant and any rent due until a new tenant moves in.</p><br /><p>\u00a0</p><br /><p><strong>Other Charges:</strong></p><br /><p><strong></strong><strong>Late Rent: </strong>If your rent is 14 days or more late, you\u2019ll be charged interest at 3% above the Bank of England base rate for every day it\u2019s overdue.</p><br /><p><strong>Lost Keys: </strong>You will have to pay for replacing lost keys or security devices. If a locksmith is needed, you\u2019ll also pay those costs, plus \u00a315 per hour for time spent replacing them.</p><br /><p><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\"><strong><br />Non-Assured Periodic Tenancy (Non-AST)</strong></span></p><br /><p>\u00a0</p><br /><p><strong>Before You Move In:</strong></p><br /><p><strong></strong><strong>Holding Deposit: </strong>Equivalent to two weeks of rent. This deposit holds the property while you complete reference checks and sign the tenancy agreement. If you cancel, provide false information, or don\u2019t complete the agreement, this deposit is not refunded.</p><br /><p><strong>Tenancy Agreement Fee:</strong> \u00a3288 (inc. VAT) for preparing the rental agreement.</p><br /><p><strong>Reference Fee: </strong>\u00a360 (inc. VAT) per person for checking your references.</p><br /><p><strong>Occupant Check Fee: </strong>\u00a330 (inc. VAT) per adult living with you, to confirm they have the legal right to rent.</p><br /><p><strong>Guarantor Fee:</strong> \u00a360 (inc. VAT) per guarantor, if one is needed to support your tenancy.</p><br /><p><strong>Security Deposit: </strong>Six weeks\u2019 rent, held in our client account, and returned if there are no issues at the end of the tenancy\u00a0</p><br /><p><strong>Stamp Duty: </strong>Applies if your rent is over \u00a3250,000 per year. Please seek independent advice.</p><br /><p>\u00a0</p><br /><p><strong>During Your Tenancy:</strong></p><br /><p><strong></strong><strong>Contract Amendment: </strong>\u00a3600 (inc. VAT) if you need to change your tenancy agreement during the lease.</p><br /><p><strong>Arrears Letter Fee: </strong>\u00a330 (inc. VAT) for each letter sent if your rent is overdue.</p><br /><p>\u00a0</p><br /><p><strong>Ending Your Tenanc</strong></p>",
